36
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,520
(Beau) Earth.

37
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:31,720
(Beau) It has been countless
millennia since this world

38
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,400
(Beau) was ruled by humans.

39
00:01:35,401 --> 00:01:38,109
(Beau) They once danced
in light, and they once

40
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:45,960
(Beau) touched the sky, opening
the doors to heaven.

41
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,720
(Beau) But in an instant, it ended.

42
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:55,660
(Beau) Alien invaders from
deep in the cosmos arrived

43
00:01:55,661 --> 00:01:59,980
(Beau) through the gates and rained
an inferno upon their garden.

44
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:05,180
(Beau) They were called dragons,
and they brought with

45
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,980
(Beau) them fire and hatred.

46
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:11,340
(Beau) But humankind fought back.

47
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:18,060
(Beau) They created battle
machines, and those machines

48
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,460
(Beau) created more machines.

49
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:25,080
(Beau) And when those machines
failed, they made pacts

50
00:02:25,081 --> 00:02:32,920
(Beau) with demons in the darkest places of the
world, and birthed unspeakable monsters.

51
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,800
(Beau) With their champions
astride them, the humans

52
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:42,040
(Beau) turned the tide of war and slew
the dragons by the thousands.

53
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:46,520
(Beau) From their husks, the
humans created engines.

54
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,680
(Beau) whose parts never rust.

55
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:53,660
(Beau) Or broke, whose pistons
operated ceaselessly, and

56
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:57,660
(Beau) whose combustion was
interminable, irradiating

57
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:01,980
(Beau) our world with mana
waves that allowed them to

58
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,540
(Beau) wield terrible magics.

59
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:13,500
(Beau) The war raged for a
century more, as humankind

60
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:17,420
(Beau) and dragonkind ground
their numbers to dust.

61
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:21,044
(Beau) The dragons summoned
the last of their spite

62
00:03:21,124 --> 00:03:24,300
(Beau) and scorched the lands
with it, and vanished.

63
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:28,940
(Beau) There only remained the
dragon engines used to

64
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:33,180
(Beau) power the last bastions
of hope in a dying world.

65
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:53,880
(Scott) If you could see past
the scars, if you could look

66
00:03:53,881 --> 00:03:59,000
(Scott) beyond the tumors and
craters, if you could peer

67
00:03:59,001 --> 00:04:02,440
(Scott) through the stinging
grit and torn soul of Nash

68
00:04:02,441 --> 00:04:08,600
(Scott) Maggard, you'd find
light—blinding, rending,

69
00:04:09,215 --> 00:04:10,840
(Scott) destructive, terrible light.

70
00:04:13,109 --> 00:04:14,109
(Scott) Look deeper.

71
00:04:15,095 --> 00:04:17,360
(Scott) And you would find a
man who could blot out the

72
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:22,880
(Scott) very sun and take this land
beyond the repair of man or machine.

73
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:27,840
(Scott) One who could bring pure
and permanent darkness

74
00:04:27,841 --> 00:04:33,360
(Scott) with his curse, taking this decaying,
festering world to its final rest.

75
00:04:36,590 --> 00:04:42,320
(Scott) But if you look yet deeper at Nash
Magard, there is more than this.

76
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,720
(Scott) You would find a spark of something like.

77
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:52,040
(Scott) salvation, something like
redemption, something

78
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:58,920
(Scott) small but able, perhaps willing to face down
the darker temptations that surround it.

79
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:05,560
(Scott) Indeed, there may yet
be a time when the name

80
00:05:05,561 --> 00:05:09,000
(Scott) Maggard is spoken in this
desolation without revulsion.

81
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:12,320
(Scott) And the flow of tears
from frightened children.

82
00:05:14,430 --> 00:05:16,640
(Scott) Perhaps there will come
a time when he will be

83
00:05:16,641 --> 00:05:19,840
(Scott) remembered as something
more, something better.

84
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:23,520
(Scott) That day is not now.

85
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:30,080
(Scott) His path is new, and his countless years
in the solar mines are well behind him.

86
00:05:31,685 --> 00:05:36,160
(Scott) In his leaving wake, there lies devastation
of the wicked and the righteous.

87
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:40,340
(Scott) His escape left none to
tell what they had seen.

88
00:05:41,365 --> 00:05:43,303
(Scott) History would never
know what happened there,

89
00:05:43,304 --> 00:05:46,500
(Scott) but Nash knew, and
that would haunt him.

90
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:51,140
(Scott) But it would also fuel
him, like the ancient oil

91
00:05:51,141 --> 00:05:54,980
(Scott) grounds did for the upright
men before the fall a millennia ago.

92
00:05:58,025 --> 00:05:59,300
(Scott) It is near dawn now.

93
00:06:00,555 --> 00:06:02,740
(Scott) He stamps out the
remains of his cookfire with

94
00:06:02,741 --> 00:06:05,620
(Scott) his tattered boot and looks
to the west with one eye.

95
00:06:07,215 --> 00:06:11,160
(Scott) The other burns, sightless
and dormant, and waits

96
00:06:11,161 --> 00:06:13,960
(Scott) for the next chance to
play its dark and terrible role.

97
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,360
(Scott) He takes his staff from
its resting place among

98
00:06:18,361 --> 00:06:20,920
(Scott) the stones, throws his
threadbare satchel over

99
00:06:20,921 --> 00:06:24,680
(Scott) his pure shoulder, and puts
the rising sun to his back.

100
00:06:27,295 --> 00:06:31,320
(Scott) He knows not who he will meet, nor
what he will face, and he doesn't care.

101
00:06:31,645 --> 00:06:33,080
(Scott) What comes will come.

102
00:06:33,735 --> 00:06:37,120
(Scott) And when it does, Nash
will be ready to face it.

103
00:06:39,605 --> 00:06:41,760
(Scott) He takes a final look
over his shoulder, back

104
00:06:41,761 --> 00:06:44,960
(Scott) toward the Blood Canyons,
the only home he'd ever known.

105
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,360
(Scott) He can never go back.

106
00:06:47,625 --> 00:06:52,160
(Scott) He knows this, and yet his heart
still aches for the one long lost.

107
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,040
(Scott) Perhaps a story for a different time.

108
00:06:57,605 --> 00:07:00,080
(Scott) His boots left dusty
footprints as he walked.

109
00:07:00,650 --> 00:07:04,660
(Scott) The only evidence that
Nash Maggard was here—they

110
00:07:04,661 --> 00:07:07,220
(Scott) would soon be blown to
oblivion by the next storm.

111
00:07:08,985 --> 00:07:14,980
(Scott) Like a chapter in the old books, his page
was turning, and he was turning with it.

112
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:18,820
(Scott) And for now, that was enough.

113
00:07:26,985 --> 00:07:28,660
(Kristen) The light fades.

114
00:07:30,015 --> 00:07:31,480
(Kristen) The vision dims.

115
00:07:32,475 --> 00:07:36,120
(Kristen) All that remains are memories.

116
00:07:36,735 --> 00:07:40,440
(Kristen) We tell of a time of
chaos, ruined dreams, this

117
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,720
(Kristen) wasted land.

118
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:48,360
(Kristen) But there are those of us that speak
of hope—the way the world could be.

119
00:07:48,925 --> 00:07:51,880
(Kristen) To recall what it was
like, we have to go back to

120
00:07:51,881 --> 00:07:57,320
(Kristen) the other time when this world was blue
and green, and the desert sprouted life.

121
00:07:58,465 --> 00:07:59,465
(Kristen) Gone now.

122
00:08:00,610 --> 00:08:01,900
(Kristen) Swept away.

123
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:06,620
(Kristen) For reasons long forgotten,
mighty dragons came

124
00:08:06,621 --> 00:08:09,740
(Kristen) from beyond and touched
off a Blaze which engulfed it all.

125
00:08:10,785 --> 00:08:13,580
(Kristen) Without a means to fight,
the humans were nothing.

126
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,380
(Kristen) They were made of naught but straw.

127
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:20,060
(Kristen) The thundering creatures
roared and pillaged.

128
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:26,540
(Kristen) Heroes fought and fought and fought,
but nothing could stem the conflagration.

129
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:34,840
(Kristen) The world crumbled, life exploded—a
whirlwind of death, a firestorm of fear.

130
00:08:35,455 --> 00:08:37,960
(Kristen) Men began to feed on men.

131
00:08:39,049 --> 00:08:44,760
(Kristen) For those that survived, it
was a nightmare with no end.

132
00:08:46,070 --> 00:08:49,480
(Kristen) Only those brave enough
to seek help, desperate

133
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:54,600
(Kristen) enough to live, would find the
demons and make the dark pact.

134
00:08:56,110 --> 00:08:59,071
(Kristen) The demons took over
the land, ready to wage

135
00:08:59,072 --> 00:09:01,470
(Kristen) war and win back the
world from the dragons.

136
00:09:01,635 --> 00:09:05,550
(Kristen) And in this maelstrom
of decay, the tieflings

137
00:09:05,551 --> 00:09:09,185
(Kristen) emerged, powerful and
strong, men and women,

138
00:09:09,186 --> 00:09:12,030
(Kristen) the warriors designed
to destroy the dragons.

139
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:20,670
(Kristen) In the roar of battle, we lost everything
and became a shell of what we were.

140
00:09:21,745 --> 00:09:25,900
(Kristen) A burnt-out, desolate
race, a race haunted by the

141
00:09:25,901 --> 00:09:30,700
(Kristen) demons of the past, a race that
wandered out into the wasteland.

142
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:37,580
(Kristen) And it was here, in this blighted
place, that we learned to live again.

143
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:43,340
(Kristen) And so began our journey to
right the wrong, to erase the past.

144
00:09:44,865 --> 00:09:48,140
(Kristen) Among us, we found a
new promise: the Tiefling

145
00:09:48,141 --> 00:09:50,540
(Kristen) who would travel back
and complete the pact.

146
00:09:51,350 --> 00:09:54,790
(Kristen) Hope, and just as my ancestral stories have

147
00:09:54,791 --> 00:09:59,030
(Kristen) foretold, I've traveled far beyond
the reach of society's misconceptions.

148
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:02,870
(Kristen) The dragon engines,
the precious engines, are

149
00:10:02,871 --> 00:10:06,390
(Kristen) hidden across the world,
and I'm going to find one.

150
00:10:06,630 --> 00:10:10,550
(Kristen) Head back to the past and
restore this world to its former glory.

151
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:12,710
(Kristen) The current wasteland.

152
00:10:14,230 --> 00:10:16,790
(Kristen) This is the last we'll ever see of it.

153
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:20,310
(Kristen) It will live on only in our memories.

154
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:29,700
(John) My name is Stanley Billings, and
I'm going to save this wasteland.

155
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:33,620
(John) Take a look around;
you'll see what I've seen my

156
00:10:33,621 --> 00:10:37,860
(John) entire life: brutality,
hopelessness, death.

157
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,500
(John) I was once right there with you.

158
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:46,020
(John) I've had my fair share of bad choices
just to see another miserable day.

159
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:50,980
(John) That all changed when
I found the artifact, an

160
00:10:50,981 --> 00:10:53,940
(John) ancient Tome of forgotten
knowledge that opened

161
00:10:53,941 --> 00:10:58,180
(John) my eyes to not only what
was but also what could be.

162
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:02,020
(John) I learned the words that
we had long forgotten,

163
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:09,060
(John) words like society, Liberty, and
the path to these ideals, government.

164
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:13,700
(John) You see, it's the lawless
nature of this world.

165
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,780
(John) That has held it in chaos for so long.

166
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:20,700
(John) All it needs is the right
person, willing to do

167
00:11:20,701 --> 00:11:24,780
(John) whatever it takes to push
that chaos back into order.

168
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:27,260
(John) Am I the man to do this?

169
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,500
(John) You bet your ass I am.

170
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:35,500
(John) After all, I'm Stanley Billings,
and I'm gonna save this wasteland.

171
00:11:40,849 --> 00:11:45,020
(Kyle) Between the rocky
crags of Veathitia and the

172
00:11:45,021 --> 00:11:49,100
(Kyle) endless wastes of Caegro,
there lives a creature

173
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:54,860
(Kyle) of untold strength and
tremendous fortitude—a

174
00:11:54,861 --> 00:11:59,740
(Kyle) raw, untamed pillar of
