00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:18,820
(Kyle) remains the last of his desert kin.

179
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:24,820
(Kyle) Seven feet tall, his gait a brawny swagger.

180
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:29,300
(Kyle) Borel now ventures towards
the dilapidated town of Dust Hill.

181
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:34,020
(Kyle) A massive, bloody haunch
of meat slung atop his

182
00:12:34,021 --> 00:12:37,860
(Kyle) broad shoulder—an
adequate trade for the life.

183
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:40,700
(Kyle) Giving waters that sustain
his desert wanderings,

184
00:12:41,605 --> 00:12:45,340
(Kyle) but fate seeks to break his isolation.

185
00:12:46,225 --> 00:12:49,100
(Kyle) The desert stars tell of great change.

186
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:54,380
(Kyle) Ancient machines and beasts
rise from their dormant slumber.

187
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:59,180
(Kyle) The world was once shaped by steel and oil.

188
